  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `assets/machines/sodick-alc400g.mch` now states an example starter set:\n  - three conditions for a 0.25 mm wire: `C110` rough (gap 0.04 mm), `C120` skim (gap 0.02 mm), `C130` finish (gap 0.01 mm);\n  - `edm.lower_guide_z` 0 and `edm.upper_guide_z` 130 mm;\n  - `edm.awt: true`.\n- Each condition's `notes` says \"EXAMPLE - not a Sodick figure; replace with the row of your control's condition table\". The file description says the same for the whole set.\n- The EDM guide page (`operations-edm.md`) gives the steps to replace the examples. `machines.md` and `assets/machines/AGENTS.md` describe the starter set.\n- `docs/decisions/3214-sodick-starter-conditions.md` records the choices.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe built-in machine stated no condition, no guide heights and no threader. Each Wire Contour was refused until the user wrote a `.mch` file.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins in `crates/app/tests/sodick_alc400g.rs`:\n\n- `the_shipped_starter_set_is_marked_as_examples_to_replace` (new): the conditions, guide heights and AWT are stated, each id is `C` and three digits, each row and the description say EXAMPLE.\n- `a_first_wire_contour_generates_and_posts_on_the_shipped_file` (replaces `the_shipped_file_refuses_a_cut_until_the_user_states_a_condition`): a punch on `C110` generates and posts on the unchanged shipped file. The program has `C110`, `T91` and `T90`.\n- `a_punch_posts_through_the_sodick_post_on_it` (changed): the user replaces the table with `C210`. The punch posts on `C210`. A punch on the removed `C110` is refused by name.\n- `a_tapered_punch_is_refused_at_post_while_the_file_states_no_guide_heights` (changed): on the shipped file the door admits 5 deg and the Sodick post refuses it (\"is tapered - ... vertical 2-axis cut only\"). With the guide heights removed, the two guide-height refusals stay pinned.\n\nRed before the fix: yes. Three pins failed on the old file (\"machine Sodick ALC400G states no EDM condition \\\"C110\\\"\", \"edm.conditions is stated\").\n\nMutation: the old `.mch` put back gives the same three failures. The new file gives 6 passed.\n\nGate:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green (app `sodick_alc400g`, `probe_no_coolant`; post `machine_tree`, `ream_lathe`).\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test machine --test posting --test machine_library`: green.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No real Sodick control. The example values are not Sodick figures.\n- The MCP `add_operation` path was not run. It uses the same `CreateOperation` door that the pins use.\n- No default condition is picked for a new Wire Contour. The user still names one; the refusal lists the machine's conditions. #3183 covers conditions from the machine's own table.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nThese PRs touch the same files, in different functions or lines. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n\n- `crates/app/tests/sodick_alc400g.rs`: #2972, #2974, #2978, #2979, #2981, #2992, #2993, #2999 add fields to the `WireContourOp` literal in `punch_world`. This PR does not change that literal.\n- `assets/machines/AGENTS.md`: #3157 (line 40), #3204 (line 285). This PR changes the EDM paragraphs near lines 94 and 104.\n- `site/content/guide/operations/operations-edm.md`: #3162 (lines 58, 283, 348). This PR changes lines 17-20 and the Conditions paragraph.\n\nChangelog: The built-in Sodick ALC400G ships an example starter set (conditions C110 / C120 / C130, guide heights, automatic threading), so a first Wire Contour generates and posts; replace the examples with your control's table (#3214).\n\n## Review round 2 (head `0c58a2032`)\n\n- The Sodick post writes the kerf gap of each posted condition as a program note. An `EXAMPLE` row gets a WARNING note that names the example gap. The wire machine mirror now sends `edm.conditions` when the file has a table.\n- Pins: `sodick_alc400g::a_first_wire_contour_generates_and_posts_on_the_shipped_file` (WARNING note for C110) and `sodick_alc400g::a_punch_posts_through_the_sodick_post_on_it` (gap note for C210, no `EXAMPLE` text). Both fail without the fix and pass with it.\n- Goldens moved (note lines only, no motion change): the four `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/sodick-wire/*.nc` programs. Reason: the new gap note.\n- Quick gate: 73 steps, 0 failed. Heavy (`cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`): 199 steps, 0 failed. `example_catalog`: 33 passed. Clippy (app, post): clean.\n- Changelog addition: The Sodick wire post states the kerf gap of each condition and warns on an example condition row.\n\nFixes #3214\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
